9},{"period":"2024-02","dataOrigin":"workbook","co2eTonnes":10.633524,"weightTonnes":97.628,"intensity":8.956,"avoidableTonnes":0.633618,"ifBestTonnes":9.999906},{"period":"2024-03","dataOrigin":"workbook","co2eTonnes":18.562106,"weightTonnes":157.097,"intensity":8.888,"avoidableTonnes":0.669186,"ifBestTonnes":17.89292},{"period":"2024-04","dataOrigin":"workbook","co2eTonnes":11.511405,"weightTonnes":82.033,"intensity":8.565,"avoidableTonnes":0.071136,"ifBestTonnes":11.440269},{"period":"2024-05","dataOrigin":"workbook","co2eTonnes":12.553109,"weightTonnes":86.765,"intensity":10.494,"avoidableTonnes":2.357238,"ifBestTonnes":10.195871},{"period":"2024-06","dataOrigin":"workbook","co2eTonnes":21.861745,"weightTonnes":169.641,"intensity":9.14,"avoidableTonnes":1.515384,"ifBestTonnes":20.346361}],"methodology":{"formula":"CO₂e (t) = distance (km) × emission factor ÷ 1,000, with weight (t) applied for rail, ocean and air.","roadBasis":"Road is charged per truck run at 0.5928 kg CO₂e/km regardless of load — the workbook's own basis.","distance":"2. Sea Port distance: Ports.com 3. Airports distance: 1. Google Maps 2. www.prokerala.com/travel/airports/distance/from-hyd/to-sea/ 4. Road Ways and Railways Distance: Google Maps","factors":"Road 0.5928 kg/km · Rail 0.00996 · Ocean 0.0084 · Air 1.58 kg per tonne-km, all as stated in the workbook.","scope":"Scope 3 · Category 9 — Downstream transportation & distribution","boundary":"First-mile collection from the growing regions, factory to inland depot, depot to gateway port, and the international sailing or flight."},"dataSourceNotes":["1. VKS data dated 19-May-2023","2. Sea Port distance: Ports.com","3. Airports distance: 1. Google Maps 2. www.prokerala.com/travel/airports/distance/from-hyd/to-sea/","4. Road Ways and Railways Distance: Google Maps","1. VKS data"],"workbookOnly":true,"assumptions":["The workbook records dispatch dates only, so transit is estimated from its distances. Every transit figure is marked \"est.\" and no CO₂e depends on one.","The workbook records FY21-22, FY22-23 and FY23-24 and stops on 2024-06-30; every row in it has already shipped. The only rows in this dataset that are not from the workbook are the 30 to-be-planned shipments — nothing between 2024-06-30 and 2026-08-01 has been filled in, so every reported figure, every chart of history and the whole ESG report are the workbook's own numbers and nothing else.","The forward book is the FY23-24 export shipments dispatched between August and December, rolled forward 3 years into the Aug–Dec 2026 planning window — 30 shipments, capped at 30 so the queue stays reviewable. It exists because the workbook has no forward-dated rows and a routing decision can only be made on a shipment that has not moved yet. Product, weight, gateway, container, every distance and every emission factor are the recorded shipment's; only the dates move, and each row carries the cell range it came from.","Route options are only offered where the workbook records every leg they use, and each shows how many shipments already moved that way.","Region and market are derived from the workbook's destination port names; product form and Scoville rating are parsed from its item descriptions.","A shipment shows at most one card per lever — shorter first mile, shorter sailing, different gateway, sea instead of air, shared truck — and only where that lever beats the route as booked. The optimised route is the lowest-CO₂e routing of those; where nothing beats the booked route, the booked route is the optimised one and the count of alternatives priced is shown instead.","Inland alternatives are drawn from all three tabs. The tabs disagree about the factory-to-depot run — 645 km on 69 FY21-22 rows against 21 km on 62 others and 51 km to \"ICD Hyderabad\" on FY23-24 — and the shorter-first-mile option names both distances rather than silently picking one."]}